Description: Nearest shrunken centroid (NSC) classifiers for high-dimensional,
    low-sample-size data such as gene expression. Implements the original
    homoscedastic NSC with soft thresholding (Prediction Analysis of
    Microarrays; Tibshirani et al. 2002 <doi:10.1073/pnas.082099299>), its
    hard- and order-thresholding versions (Sahtout, Wang and Ghimire 2024
    <doi:10.1080/03610918.2022.2047201>), and
    the heteroscedastic extension of Sahtout and Wang that uses class-specific
    variances in both the test statistic and the discriminant function
    (methods STh3, HTh3 and OTh3). The thresholding parameter is selected by a
    refined ("deep") cross-validation search. Also provides the simulation
    design, per-class performance metrics and the relative-heterogeneity
    diagnostic used in the paper.
